WEBVTT

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.570
Such unpleasant weather.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.080
Principal!

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.710
No...

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.180
I can't! I mustn't share it!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.210
But...

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.210
Miss Yoshinoya?

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.470
I've been saving it!

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.290
Oh, but if it's only that far, it doesn't count.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:54.700
Tight fit.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:56.990
It's not like that!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.950
This is just a coincidence!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.450
A youthful indiscretion!

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.730
What...

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:29.730
June 5th
"Matchstick Mystery"

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.040
So, what you wanna do?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.370
The weather's too bad to go out. They said it was going to keep raining all day.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.120
Why does it have to rain on our day off?

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.120
Matchstick
y
s
t
e
r
y

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.120
Can you solve this mystery?

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.630
If you're curious, the answer is on the web!

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.260
Coming.

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.550
Oh, it's you guys.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.080
It's booting up now.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.170
Okay, Yuno, here's the mouse.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.240
Thanks.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.630
Huh?

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.510
Nori, did I break it!?

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.140
Just hold on a bit until it finishes booting.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.220
So, what did they say to search for?

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.480
Um... matchstick mystery.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.650
Yeah, the commercial said the answer was on the web.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:53.650
This?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.280
Yeah, that's it.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.530
Matchstick
Mystery

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:56.280
Make the kanji 田 using
only four matchsticks!

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:56.280
Remember, no bending
or breaking them!!!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.530
Here!!!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.530
Stack them like this,
and there's your 田!

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:00.610
That's it?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.450
Matchstick
Mystery

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.450
Here!!!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.450
Stack them like this,
and there's your 田!

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.470
Horrible! That's horrible!

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.250
Curse you, internets!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.540
Is this internet criticism?

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:18.060
Sorry to bother you about that.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.680
Well sure, I guess.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.270
You don't have much in your room, do you, Nori?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.820
You keep it nice and simple.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:36.570
Yeah, no reason to have things scattered all over.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.730
Wow, a Furbo! Does it still talk? Does it?

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.750
It's not like I keep it because I think it's cute or anything!

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.550
Norippe, did you buy your computer at an electronics store?

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.870
Was it expensive?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.760
Not sure.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.840
I don't know how much it cost.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.640
My uncle built it for me as a gift for starting high school.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.130
Your uncle...

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:06.890
...built it?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.390
Wow.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.890
Nori, is your uncle Mr. Gates?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.270
No way!

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:20.620
Well, when I say he built it, it's more like he put it together.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.910
Do you mind if I use your computer a little more?

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.160
Sure, go ahead.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.290
This screen's the desktop.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.630
Nori, can I open this?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.590
You're gonna drive me crazy asking these things.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.150
If you wanna go online, just use this like you did before.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.260
Why don't we look at Yamabuki's page?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.520
WHEEEE
WHEEEE
WHEEEE

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.520
WHEE

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.520
It's the principal!

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:58.520
You can scroll using the clicky wheel in the middle.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.760
There's a list of the teachers too.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.910
I've never looked there before.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:13.350
I wonder what'll come up if we search for their full names.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:15.870
I want to see what comes up for Miss Yoshinoya!

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.760
It's gotta just be someone with the same name.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:27.300
Yeah, someone with the same name.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.130
You must be hungry. Why don't we order a pizza?

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:39.820
Sure.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.190
Mind if I grab the chair?

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:47.200
You guys are fine with Turin Pizza, right? What toppings do you want?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.490
You can order from a computer?

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.200
Nazuna, what do you want?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.830
That one looks like it would be good.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.420
I want to try it too!

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.010
All right, there we go!

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.880
What, that's all it takes?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:09.220
What if you accidentally order when you just came to look at the pizzas?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.970
Who's gonna go just to look?

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.980
This is great!

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:21.220
Great pick, Nazuna.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.860
Thanks.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.240
Hold on a sec.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.700
It's from a friend back home.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.730
It's like a phone you use online.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.040
You can even do that with a computer?

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.750
Hello, Miho?

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.970
Sorry, ya caught me with the girls at my place.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.250
A Kansai dialect!?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.090
What're y'all so surprised 'bout?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:53.510
Oh, right, you want to try CG? It's fun.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.640
CG? Computer graphics?

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.300
You draw just like this.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:10.380
There's lots of brushes, and each has a different texture.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:12.950
SGI!

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.620
Amazing? [sugoi]

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.330
Yeah.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.870
Wouldn't it be faster just to say it normally?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.630
This is fun! And it's so easy to color.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:29.550
Ain't it?

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:34.220
Sorry!

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:38.850
I just thought it was great that you were drawing right in front of me.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.150
Really? Thanks.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.110
Take as many as you like.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.110
Thank you.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:51.840
Now, to make it my wallpaper.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.450
Okay, that's embarrassing.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:59.710
Hey, Nazuna, why did you come over anyway?

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.330
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:10.340
Well, Yuno and Miyako came right after you, so I forgot all about it.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.510
What was it?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:14.510
I'm already done.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:18.020
I just wanted to have lunch with you.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:21.650
Nazuna!

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:23.020
Sorry!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.360
Um, sorry to bother you.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.690
Oh, don't worry.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:35.110
It was fun going online and drawing. Do you mind if I use it again some time?

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.910
Go right ahead. I had fun too.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:43.750
Anyway, are you done for the day? Can I go ahead and shut down Windows?

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.170
Out the window?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.050
It's fine! I'll do it later!

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.200
Hey, Nori, are you in?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.390
Oh, everyone's here.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.600
Hey, Sae, Hiro!

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.430
Hello.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.980
What's up?

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.530
Sorry to bother you all of a sudden.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:13.320
We just saw the matchstick quiz on TV, and we wanted to look up the answer.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.780
Oh, sorry.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.160
I haven't shut the computer down yet, so good—

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.790
Hold on a minute.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:29.380
The whole point is to sharpen your mind and change your perspective.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.630
She's lecturing them!?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.330
No way that's the answer.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.600
All right, I'm shutting it down then.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.350
We saw the answer earlier too.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.560
Miya got all angry about it.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:51.280
Okay then, how do you make four equilateral triangles with six matches?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:55.020
Quit changing the subject, Miyako.

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.720
The rain's finally cleared up.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:25.630
The rainy season usually finishes along with exams, right?

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:27.690
There's still a while left.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:32.880
But the seasons change before you even notice.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.570
Look away, and they'll pass in the blink of an eye.

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:40.570
February 16th

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:40.570
"48.5cm"

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.920
It looks a bit chilly today.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.280
Yunocchi! You up?

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.280
Yeah.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:25.040
Hurry up, Yunocchi!

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:28.120
Sorry I'm late, Miya.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.540
Sae! Hiro!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.550
Good morning!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:37.300
Oh, good morning.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.800
Good morning.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:46.340
I guess it's not going to warm up anytime soon.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.730
The cold really does bother you.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:50.980
I'm sure it'll break soon.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.110
That's right, it's almost spring.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.860
A transfer student!?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.490
Wow, they're huge.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.870
That must be one of the third years' graduation projects.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:09.900
Graduation project?

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.540
Yeah. Every year, the third years do them around now.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:16.880
It's to let them cool down from entrance exams, so it's optional.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.340
The universities don't take them into account,

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:22.720
so there's no time limit and they don't have to be displayed anywhere in particular.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:26.680
You can ask to put them wherever you'd like.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.010
It sounds fun.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:33.440
I see. I thought they were too big for a first year.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.900
Maybe you should explain that one again.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:46.450
Now that I know they're all over, I can't stop looking for them.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:47.660
I think this is one.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.370
This ad must be one too.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.630
That's a real ad, Yunocchi.

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:02.100
This fire extinguisher has to be one.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.260
That's a normal fire extinguisher, Miya.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.730
It makes everything seem like a work of art.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.280
The world is full of art.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:27.160
The graduation projects are starting to sprout up.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:31.790
This is a wonderful, old tradition at Yamabuki.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:38.710
The school doesn't require it at all, so it's a hundred percent their own initiative.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:44.340
I hope you all can appreciate how much effort and creativity went into them.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:47.760
So, I've decided to make one too.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.390
I'm a herald of spring!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:57.020
Ah, so short, a flower's life!

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:05.020
Okay, let's finish a little early today.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.300
Viva half days!

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.120
You wanna eat lunch here?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:16.000
Sure. After we eat, why don't we look around campus a bit?

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.310
Roger!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:23.000
Ding-dong, ding-dong!

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.440
Miss Yoshinoya...

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.010
You're gonna get graduated.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:35.520
Good day. This is Todo, president of the Yamabuki High Broadcasting Club.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:38.020
How many have you found, Sae?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.570
Seven, counting Yoshinoya's attempt at a bell.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.030
So in other words, six?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.070
Was last year like this too?

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:51.280
Yeah, the atmosphere was the same.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.800
Misato's was great.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.040
That one scared me.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:03.010
They had to close the girls' bathroom on the second floor for two weeks because of it.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:05.550
What kind of work could it have been?

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.950
I wonder what we'll be working on a year from now.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.770
I hope we'll have made some progress.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.790
The huge shoes on top of the shoe lockers this morning were great.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.730
I hope I can make something that unique.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.550
That's right.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:29.240
They're going to graduate next year.

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.990
Sae! Why don't you make yourself some big boobs?

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:34.370
Miyako!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.420
Okay, we're heading home now.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:41.670
See you later.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.670
Sure.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.450
C'mon, Yuno, let's go look at the exhibits!

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:51.950
Okay.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.170
Do you understand what you did wrong?

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.010
Yes.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:12.230
Will you stop corrupting minors while on school grounds?

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:17.370
I'll try, but I don't know if I'll be able to.

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:24.470
You need to be conscious of your place as a teacher.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:28.000
More importantly, though, keep being creative.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:36.010
I have to admit, making clothing out of actual flower petals is an interesting idea.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:44.310
Wow, this is so well made!

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.020
Yeah!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:55.890
It's hard to believe students here at Yamabuki just like us made these.

00:16:55.890 --> 00:17:00.540
They're on a different level from the Yamabuki Fair.

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:05.010
It's their last work as high school students,

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:07.290
so they must be contemplating something different.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.130
I guess we'll be making these in another two years.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:13.630
Nah, there's no way we'll graduate.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.330
A little to the right.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.390
Thanks.

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.400
Arisawa!

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.770
Oh my god!

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:41.380
Yuno! I made it into college!

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:42.830
Congratulations!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:47.830
Thanks. I was able to take it easy during entrance exams,

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:51.090
and then have fun working on my graduation project.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.760
Sorry to distract you while you're—

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:06.460
Hey Yuno, why don't we swap e-mail addresses?

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.850
Of course!

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.700
I remember that phone.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.970
That's right.

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:16.700
Come on, Arisa, help out!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.610
Okay.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:21.200
Well Yuno, later.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.120
Yeah, later.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:26.710
See you.

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:33.140
That was nice, Yunocchi.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:36.010
Thanks. And sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.890
Want to look around a bit more?

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:40.140
No, I'm fine for today.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:44.020
Then let's go home, Miss Second Year.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:55.860
That's right. We're going to be second years.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:00.780
What do you want to do for dinner, Boss?

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:01.870
Boss!?

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:27.140
Once the older girls graduate, they'll be gone.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.890
It'll be lonely.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.270
But...

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:39.330
Soon, we'll be the older girls, so I've got to keep trying.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.620
February 16th

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.620
The end

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.620
To be continued

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:48.710
Five

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:49.710
Four

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:50.710
Three

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:51.710
Two

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:52.710
One

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:58.630
March 7th

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:58.630
Spring

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.450
The weather's great today.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.440
Miya!

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:25.450
The cherry blossoms are beautiful.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.670
Yeah.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:34.260
Congratulations on graduating.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.920
March 7th
Spring

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.920
The end

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.920
To be continued

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:47.180
Wow...

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:43.470
Let's name the three top secrets of Hidamari Apartments!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.240
Cuckoos perch on my balcony!

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.300
Ever since I moved here, I've been waking up early!

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:48.990
I found horsetails in the garden!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.680
That's the
evening
star.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:54.680
It's
pretty...

00:20:48.990 --> 00:20:51.480
I can hear everything that happens in Miya's room.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.390
Breakfast tastes great every day!

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.640
Isn't that the same anywhere?

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.020
For me, it's the starry sky I see out my window.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:21:02.190
Tomorrow
will be
sunny too.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:01.420
When I can't take it anymore, it cheers me up.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:05.550
Next time, "July 12th: Three Stars × Lycopene."

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:09.770
Yeah!

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:09.770
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
